@layout()
<div style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4);">
  <a href="/help">&larr; Back to Help</a>
</div>

<article class="card">
  <header>
    <h3>Import</h3>
  </header>

  <p>
    SpeakerWindows supports importing highlights from several popular reading apps. Use the
    <code>sw-importer</code>
    CLI tool to convert and upload your data.
  </p>

  <h4>Readwise</h4>
  <p>Export your highlights from Readwise as a CSV file, then run:</p>
  <pre><code>API_TOKEN=&lt;token&gt; ./sw-importer --importer=readwise highlights.csv</code></pre>

  <h4>KOReader</h4>
  <p>Export your highlights from KOReader as JSON (<code>one.json</code> or <code>all.json</code>), then run:</p>
  <pre><code>API_TOKEN=&lt;token&gt; ./sw-importer --importer=koreader highlights.json</code></pre>

  <h4>Google Play Books</h4>
  <p>Export your notes as HTML or DOCX, then run:</p>
  <pre><code>API_TOKEN=&lt;token&gt; ./sw-importer --importer=playbooks notes.html</code></pre>

  <h4>Kindle</h4>
  <p>Export your Kindle PDF notes, then run:</p>
  <pre><code>API_TOKEN=&lt;token&gt; ./sw-importer --importer=kindle notes.pdf</code></pre>

  <h4>Preview Before Importing</h4>
  <p>
    Add the <code>--print</code> flag to any command to preview the JSON output without posting to the server:
  </p>
  <pre><code>API_TOKEN=&lt;token&gt; ./sw-importer --importer=readwise --print highlights.csv</code></pre>
</article>
@end
